ts -2; Presence/Manipulation failures become dramatic failures. Intimidation and Subterfuge unaffected."},{"name":"Plague of Purity","effect":"Touch by Integrity 8+ mortal causes (10 - Humanity) bashing damage."}],"xp_log":{"earned":{"game":1},"spent":{"attributes":0,"skills":0,"merits":14,"powers":24,"special":0}},"humanity_base":7,"ordeals":[{"name":"questionnaire","complete":true},{"name":"history","complete":true},{"name":"rules","complete":true},{"name":"lore","complete":true},{"name":"covenant","complete":true}],"clan_attribute":"Composure","attribute_priorities":{"Mental":"Secondary","Physical":"Tertiary","Social":"Primary"},"skill_priorities":{"Mental":"Secondary","Physical":"Tertiary","Social":"Primary"},"bp_creation":{"cp":5},"_ots_covenant_bonus":0,"_ots_free_dots":0},{"_id":"69d73ea49162ece35897a47c","name":"Alice Vunder","player":"Katherine H","clan":"Mekhet","bloodline":null,"covenant":"Circle of the Crone","mask":"Follower","dirge":"Scholar","court_title":"Regent","concept":"Curious archivist","pronouns":"she/her","apparent_age":null,"honorific":"Regent","moniker":null,"features":null,"retired":false,"blood_potency":1,"humanity":6,"humanity_base":7,"status":{"city":2,"clan":1,"covenant":2},"covenant_standings":{"Crone":2},"attributes":{"Intelligence":{"dots":4,"bonus":0,"cp":2,"xp":0,"free":2,"rule_key":"intelligence"},"Wits":{"dots":3,"bonus":0,"cp":2,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"wits"},"Resolve":{"dots":2,"bonus":0,"cp":1,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"resolve"},"Strength":{"dots":1,"bonus":0,"cp":0,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"strength"},"Dexterity":{"dots":3,"bonus":0,"cp":2,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"dexterity"},"Stamina":{"dots":2,"bonus":0,"cp":1,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"stamina"},"Presence":{"dots":3,"bonus":1,"cp":2,"xp":0},"Manipulation":{"dots":2,"bonus":0,"cp":1,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"manipulation"},"Composure":{"dots":2,"bonus":0,"cp":1,"xp":0,"free":1,"rule_key":"composure"}},"skills":{"Academics":{"dots":2,"bonus":0,"specs":["research"],"nine_again":false,"cp":2,"xp":0,"free":0,"rule_key":"academics"},"Computer":{"dots":3,"bonus":0,"specs":["hacking"],"nine_again":false,"cp":3,"xp":0,"free":0,"rule_key":"computer"},"Investigation":{"dots":3,"bonus":0,"specs":[],"nine_again":false,"cp":3,"xp":0,"free":0,"rule_key":"investigation"},"Occult":{"dots":3,"bonus":0,"sp…209751 tokens truncated…onal_story_text": "Carver asks James to take him somewhere that is special to him. Somewhere where James feels is a \"core memeory\".",
server\scripts\_dt3-submissions.json:8540:   "project_3_description": "On becoming aware of the existence of an old necropolis Xavier starts the search to find it. He reaches out through his various contacts (foreign and domestic) to look for clues to where it might have been. Searched information on subterranean areas across the history of the city (maps, plans, geological surveys). looking for unusual gaps to information about it being accessed (especially old areas that had been more recently accessed during the time vampires were absent from the city). Looking for folklore about usual events linked to these subterranean sites and immediate surrounds.",
server\scripts\_dt3-submissions.json:9532:    "outcome_summary": "You get wind of a special deceased estate auction of a person who is reputed to be a bon fide soothsayer. You wonder how credible it is, Vaucluse is not known for mystics."
server\scripts\_dt3-submissions.json:10302:      "text": "It's all good in the hood, especially the parties.",
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:155:    "description": "Reed is looking to improve security around his haven, especially with moving to a new building. He is looking to also make some remotely controlled doors and blinds to help move in and around during the day."
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:264:    "description": "The network of influence in Politics and Finance that is the MMN cult reaps its rewards in greased palms. The right bribe, the right contract, the right environmental report. Volia - whole chunks of subterranean tunnels sealed off with special works here - accidental concrete spill there, sealed off for the M11 tunnel. Tunnels, mostly bare, ugly, damp, infested. But directly underneath and nowhere all at once! It is a patchwork of forgotten RTA service tunnels, WW2 shuttered ammunition tunnels, redundant storm-water catchment sumps, etc... It is not ownership per se. It is sealing the entry points off little clusters and burying them administratively so they are nobody's business."
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:270:   "aspirations": "Yusuf feels isolated and unsupported. The Mammon Cult (MMN) is in formative stage, but I dont really have any surety to bother building it up just for someone else to take. At the same time I have not been subtle with its presence. The cult served its initial purpose - the contrivance to get me to Sydney. It stands out as a target. Perhaps I will set it up at this stage as a honey-pot to lure investigation and actions of other kindred. I see the cult as a presently useful expendable asset.\n\nI am guest everywhere, marginalised even in the Covenant. Yusuf has a job here in Sydney - to protect Brandy. But he sees both her and Eve witless puppets on a string of more organised powers. A dangerous predicament. Yusuf must help himself first. Hence taking OBS5. And working on his lair. Mt plans are to get safe and embedded. This court seems like a dangerours and specially curated fishbowl designed to fail. I worry about the consequences for the Carthian Movement. I fear we have been trojan horsed by Eve with a plan to humiliate the movement on the global stage as the \"Carthian Experiment\" fails spectacularly.\n\nIt is unlikely building clan status within the Carthians will be viable. They are riven, misguided and working against their own interests. Eve has already cleverly seen to that. Handing out boons to those who are giddy with the proximity to praxis and ignoring those not actively bending knee. The younger Carthians in the movement seem enthusiastic to embrace a \"lets see hoe THEY like it attitude, rather than a lets do this properly\".\n\nThe City status game is meta-unstable and already stitched up. There are inner and outer cliques quickly forming and Yusuf sees no way into the inner cliques. So Yusuf must build.... \nwith what he has left in the space left to him. THE SEWERS.\n\nThe sewers and catacombs in the territory no one bothered wanting... with his Clan - the Nosferatu.  There are not many Nos, and they don't usually play well - not with others and not with themselves. I will make a place in the catacombs. I will open it to others of my kind. I will see who will come to the Necropolis once it is built. The first bricks are laid in this downtime.\n\nSHORT: GET MYSELF SAFE\nMEDIUM: BUILD THE NOS, PROTECT MMN\nLONG: NECROPOLIS UNDER THEIR FEET"
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:432:    "description": "Project Name: Who do I call?\nCharacters involved: me and Yusuf\nMerits & Bonuses:\nXP Spend: n/a\nProject description: Yusuf asked if I could help him find a connection to get some mil spec surveillance cameras. Fortunately (as he well knew…) I know a guy from my time in the military and the professional connections I have maintained back in the US. I called around and got him a name of someone who could help him out. He is so lucky he has me around…again grand ideas are one thing but landing it is my speciality."
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:467:    "description": "Project Name:  The Panopticon\nCharacters involved: Just me\nMerits & Bonuses:  Trained Observer\nXP spend: n/a\nProject Description: \n\nJack has been tasked with securing the venue for Court on April 18th. He applies his skills as a director to surveil Court.  \n\nThrough his High Society Allies, he negotiates permission from the owner (acquired for $25M in 2024) of a The Hub Theatre (shuttered and closed in 1996) on King Street in Newtown to allow him to put on a small exhibit for a dry run of a private viewing (Court), which he intends to repeat as an extended special exhibit during next DT for high society members (Moulding Room shenanigans). \n\n[full description of Court setup will be sent to STs] \nThe Exhibit consists of projectors with small screens and seats arranged around the art deco ballroom of the theatre profiling visual media over the past century of the Theatre's history -- vaudeville, silent movies, early black and white, colorised film, porn productions in the 70s/80s, and ultimately nothing from ~1996 onwards. The Final Exhibit shows a live feed, top down, of a camera with a LENSBABY Composer 2 Pro Bending Camera Lens mounted on the ceiling that shows the movement of Kindred around the ballroom, blurred focus around the edges by clear focus on the centre -- which is where the central seat for the Premier is located. [Primary dice pool to set up]\n\nWith his Eye Behind the Glass detournement active (on a camera in his Haven watching the feed from Court), Jack would be able to constantly keep an eye on that central spot of Court (who is talking to the Premier, and for how long) and gain some insights on the machinations of Court. [Secondary dice pool]"
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:544:    "description": "Project Name: A Strange Occurence\nCharacters involved: Cazz, Lucinda \nMerits & Bonuses: \nXP Spend: n/a\nProject description: Cazz and Lucinda met up at UNSW earlier in the month, to talk privately about the shared 'bad vibes' felt across Sydney the month prior. During Court, it was discovered at least three other vampires felt this, across multiple territories. So, who was Cazz not to follow an interesting thing?\nLucinda seems to be better at actual investigations, so, Cazz thought to start with their speciality, dipping into their specific Occult knowledge. And its always good to get a lay of the lines anyway, ey?"
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:550:    "description": "Project Name: Second City Vibe Check\nCharacters involved: Just me\nMerits & Bonuses:  Face In The Crowd\nXP Spend: n/a\nProject description: Cazz usually spents time in the Academy. The Second City is a whole new area to see what the area is like, who stays here, who doesn't, and try to not be noticed too hard. Don't need to show up and be loud, especially if we Carthains are gonna look after this place. Ooh, and there's a University here! Excellent. Whose here?"
server\scripts\_dt2-submissions.json:579:    "description": "Project Name: Keeping it Tight\nCharacters involved: Me and Mac (Also: Jack, Keeper, Anichka, Cyrus) \nMerits and Bonuses: N/A\nXP Spent: N/A\nProject Description: I’ve been invited by Jack to patrol the Academy for poachers and interlopers, which I’ll certainly do, but what I’m really interested in is information. Last month I learned from my political contacts that the Academy is ‘on the radar’. I’d like to see if there’s anything I could match to that information. Any places that look like they could use the investment of the Covenant that’s to be looking after this territory. And especially, anything that directly contradicts the information that I already have. All this with an eye to being able to make intelligent, evidenced recommendations to Jack next Court."
