public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4035:        "standout_rp": "The new fellow in the red suit is amazing, especially for their first game. Also Yusuf Kronkshuc (Peter) for impecible Nos roleplay and costuming- Above and beyond, the only Nos I know at a glance.",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4036:        "ic_correspondence": "Solidarity\n\nI've sent a list of names accompanying this missive, these are the Kindred important enough to attend court in Sydney. Territory is being divided, my fellow Carthians placing me in power over one of them for the moment- 'The Second city'. The cycle of Kindred dominance is spinning up. The silver lining at least, is that our fledgling Premier seemingly wants to do something all-together unique with the city. Obviously this is extremely confidential, but I'm an Anti-Obstructionist first, and a Carthian second. \n\nHer plan: To institute a rule- though both Carthian Law and practical enforcement, to preclude all but the least blood-potent kindred entrance into the city. \n\nOn one hand, this would bar those with extreme powers of the blood and the appetites that accompany them. On the other, it does encourage kindred to lean more heavily on their more mortal-facing powers. Then again, less potency means less blood to influence mortals with. I'm undecided about this, but probably have more pertinent issues to navigate.\n\nI've set up some roots in addition to the new territory, a public radio station and some informants in mortal affairs- though I worry many of the institutions of the city have been taken solidly by kindred, especially in the finance sector. I've also spoken more with the Crone member known as 'Alice Vunder'. They have a rather Anti-Obstructionist viewpoint. We've reached an understanding, and perhaps with a bit of a push, I can make a radical out of her. Then again, you never know with witches. \n\nI am, as ever, surrounded by cut-throat predators. I feel somewhat like a seagull in a hurricane.\n\nCest la vie. Mieux vaut être chanceux que bon.\n\n~R",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4187:      "correspondence": "Solidarity\n\nI've sent a list of names accompanying this missive, these are the Kindred important enough to attend court in Sydney. Territory is being divided, my fellow Carthians placing me in power over one of them for the moment- 'The Second city'. The cycle of Kindred dominance is spinning up. The silver lining at least, is that our fledgling Premier seemingly wants to do something all-together unique with the city. Obviously this is extremely confidential, but I'm an Anti-Obstructionist first, and a Carthian second. \n\nHer plan: To institute a rule- though both Carthian Law and practical enforcement, to preclude all but the least blood-potent kindred entrance into the city. \n\nOn one hand, this would bar those with extreme powers of the blood and the appetites that accompany them. On the other, it does encourage kindred to lean more heavily on their more mortal-facing powers. Then again, less potency means less blood to influence mortals with. I'm undecided about this, but probably have more pertinent issues to navigate.\n\nI've set up some roots in addition to the new territory, a public radio station and some informants in mortal affairs- though I worry many of the institutions of the city have been taken solidly by kindred, especially in the finance sector. I've also spoken more with the Crone member known as 'Alice Vunder'. They have a rather Anti-Obstructionist viewpoint. We've reached an understanding, and perhaps with a bit of a push, I can make a radical out of her. Then again, you never know with witches. \n\nI am, as ever, surrounded by cut-throat predators. I feel somewhat like a seagull in a hurricane.\n\nCest la vie. Mieux vaut être chanceux que bon.\n\n~R",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4191:      "rp_shoutout": "[\"The new fellow in the red suit is amazing\",\"especially for their first game. Also Yusuf Kronkshuc (Peter) for impecible Nos roleplay and costuming- Above and beyond\",\"the only Nos I know at a glance.\"]",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4762:          "description": "Project Name: Who do I call?\nCharacters involved: me and Yusuf\nMerits & Bonuses:\nXP Spend: n/a\nProject description: Yusuf asked if I could help him find a connection to get some mil spec surveillance cameras. Fortunately (as he well knew…) I know a guy from my time in the military and the professional connections I have maintained back in the US. I called around and got him a name of someone who could help him out. He is so lucky he has me around…again grand ideas are one thing but landing it is my speciality.",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4768:          "detail": "Characters involved: me and Yusuf\nMerits & Bonuses:\nProject description: Yusuf asked if I could help him find a connection to get some mil spec surveillance cameras. Fortunately (as he well knew…) I know a guy from my time in the military and the professional connections I have maintained back in the US. I called around and got him a name of someone who could help him out. He is so lucky he has me around…again grand ideas are one thing but landing it is my speciality."
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:4827:      "project_4_description": "Characters involved: me and Yusuf\nMerits & Bonuses:\nProject description: Yusuf asked if I could help him find a connection to get some mil spec surveillance cameras. Fortunately (as he well knew…) I know a guy from my time in the military and the professional connections I have maintained back in the US. I called around and got him a name of someone who could help him out. He is so lucky he has me around…again grand ideas are one thing but landing it is my speciality.",
public\mockups\data\downtime_submissions.json:5473:        "st_response": "The outfit is nothing special: black compression top, dark cargo trousers, a bandana knotted across the eyes. Off the internet. It does not make you look heroic. This is the point.\n\nYou work a circuit through the Dockyard across four nights, finding the people who keep other people indoors and relocating them to someone else's problem. The conversations are brief. Close enough that they can smell what they are dealing with, and they make sensible decisions. Word moves through the district in the way it always does in places where people pay attention to who comes and goes.\n\nBy the end of the month something has shifted in the small hours. More lights on. People taking the direct route to early shifts rather than the long way round. The territory is still itself: unglamorous, salt-smelling, working. Something has been cleared out of it.",
