server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:6445:            "description": "Project Name: The Panopticon\nCharacters involved: Just me\nMerits & Bonuses: Trained Observer\nXP spend: n/a\nProject Description: \n\nJack has been tasked with securing the venue for Court on April 18th. He applies his skills as a director to surveil Court. \n\nThrough his High Society Allies, he negotiates permission from the owner (acquired for $25M in 2024) of a The Hub Theatre (shuttered and closed in 1996) on King Street in Newtown to allow him to put on a small exhibit for a dry run of a private viewing (Court), which he intends to repeat as an extended special exhibit during next DT for high society members (Moulding Room shenanigans). \n\n[full description of Court setup will be sent to STs] \nThe Exhibit consists of projectors with small screens and seats arranged around the art deco ballroom of the theatre profiling visual media over the past century of the Theatre's history -- vaudeville, silent movies, early black and white, colorised film, porn productions in the 70s/80s, and ultimately nothing from ~1996 onwards. The Final Exhibit shows a live feed, top down, of a camera with a LENSBABY Composer 2 Pro Bending Camera Lens mounted on the ceiling that shows the movement of Kindred around the ballroom, blurred focus around the edges by clear focus on the centre -- which is where the central seat for the Premier is located. [Primary dice pool to set up]\n\nWith his Eye Behind the Glass detournement active (on a camera in his Haven watching the feed from Court), Jack would be able to constantly keep an eye on that central spot of Court (who is talking to the Premier, and for how long) and gain some insights on the machinations of Court. [Secondary dice pool]",
