server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:17685:        "outcome_text": "## Feeding\nPredatory — stalks solitary souls through Sydney streets at night; uses patience and a Mekhet's eye for detail to isolate prey\nDexterity + Stealth (Stalking speciality) — 7 dice\nThe Dockyard — The Dockyard — 0\n\n## Projects\n### The Temptation of Eve\nThe invitation to Eve Lockridge's company headquarters was a gift you had not expected, and you had no intention of wasting it.\nYou walk the perimeter of LHL Transport in the small hours, night after night, until you know it the way you know a psalm: the rhythm of arrivals and departures, where the light holds and where it does not, the loading dock that is busiest at hours that have nothing to do with freight.\nThe company is structured to resist exactly this kind of scrutiny — not accidentally, not through negligence, but by design. The audit trail folds back on itself in ways that suggest professional assistance. The operation is real. It is also obscured. What it is obscuring is still ahead of you. How unprofessional would using Twilight Projection really be…\n\n### Les Misérables\nRene Meyer is not easy to watch.\nYou spent weeks turning over what little you had from Court — the shape of her, the way she moved through a room, the fact of her — and finding no thread to pull. The city is large and she left no obvious trail.\nWhat broke it open was the radio. Late at night, scanning frequencies out of habit: a show, ostensibly crime and safety awareness, carrying the quality of something made by someone who knows exactly what they are constructing. You placed the voice on the third listen. Worked backward from the transmission source. Followed it as far as it would go this month, which was further than you had any right to expect.\nYou have a location now. Not where she sleeps — that remains ahead of you — but where she works, and something of how she moves. It is enough to continue from.\n\n### Brandy Old Fashioned\nShe is harder to find than expected.\nThree weeks of careful enquiries through the right channels and she never resolves into anything solid — no haven, no pattern, no address. Then: a name, attached to a description, attached to a circuit of fundraisers and gallery openings she has apparently been working with considerable purpose. The people who mention her do so with the particular warmth of those who have been charmed recently. She is visible in certain rooms. You have not been in those rooms. You know she exists in them.\nIt is a beginning. She is someone who knows how to be present without being knowable, and you have enough respect for that to proceed carefully.\n\n### Mister Cellophane\nObfuscate is the logical extension of everything you already do. You have spent decades learning how to be unremarkable, how to occupy a room without registering in it, how to ask questions in ways that do not feel like questions. This is simply that, made permanent.\nSeeing your grandsire again reminded you that not all threats announce themselves, and some things are better faced invisible.\n\n## Merit Actions\n### Action 1\nThe contact takes three days to respond. When he does, it is careful.\n\n## Touchstone\nYou know Elise's route now. You tell yourself this is because you are a careful man who observes carefully, which is true, but it is not why you are here.\nElise stops to look at something in a shop window and the light catches the angle of her jaw and your chest does the thing it has been doing since you first saw her, a kind of seizing that should not be possible in something without a heartbeat. Her name is not Astrid. You know her name is not Astrid. You have been telling yourself this for six months and it has not helped at all.\nElise turns the key in her door and goes inside and the light comes on and you walk away before you do something you cannot take back.\n\n## Letter\nDear Conrad,\n\nPrimogen. Yes. I read your letter twice to be certain I had understood correctly.\n\nI will not pretend I did not expect the Sheriff's office to be yours. You expected it too, which is why you have written to me in the language of acceptance rather than the language of satisfaction. I know the difference. I have been reading your letters for a very long time.\n\nThe question I would put to you is not whether you will honour the position (of course you will; you are incapable of doing otherwise) but whether you will allow yourself to want what is actually in front of you, rather than mourning what is not. Primogen is not nothing. In a city this new, it may be everything.\n\nGod's plans and ours rarely align on the first attempt. This is not news to either of us.\n\nYour affectionate mentor,\nDr Flanders\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Dockyard\nThere is something wrong with the animals this month.\nYou notice it on the first night — a particular quality of restlessness in the creatures near the waterfront, a tension that runs through them like a current. By the third week the docks themselves are disrupted. Workers complaining at shift change, operations running short, an energy in the air that makes people move faster and speak less. The blood here is thin; you leave each feeding with less than you came for, which is not new for this territory, but the degree of it is.\nYou are not the only one working these streets, and this month that has been unusually visible. Two figures, over several nights — Doc, who walks like she owns the ground she is standing on, and Macheath, who watches everything she cannot. They made no attempt at concealment. The opposite, in fact. Whatever they were doing in the Dockyard, they wanted it noticed.\nCarthians. You know the type.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:17730:      "published_outcome": "## Feeding\nPredatory — stalks solitary souls through Sydney streets at night; uses patience and a Mekhet's eye for detail to isolate prey\nDexterity + Stealth (Stalking speciality) — 7 dice\nThe Dockyard — The Dockyard — 0\n\n## Projects\n### The Temptation of Eve\nThe invitation to Eve Lockridge's company headquarters was a gift you had not expected, and you had no intention of wasting it.\nYou walk the perimeter of LHL Transport in the small hours, night after night, until you know it the way you know a psalm: the rhythm of arrivals and departures, where the light holds and where it does not, the loading dock that is busiest at hours that have nothing to do with freight.\nThe company is structured to resist exactly this kind of scrutiny — not accidentally, not through negligence, but by design. The audit trail folds back on itself in ways that suggest professional assistance. The operation is real. It is also obscured. What it is obscuring is still ahead of you. How unprofessional would using Twilight Projection really be…\n\n### Les Misérables\nRene Meyer is not easy to watch.\nYou spent weeks turning over what little you had from Court — the shape of her, the way she moved through a room, the fact of her — and finding no thread to pull. The city is large and she left no obvious trail.\nWhat broke it open was the radio. Late at night, scanning frequencies out of habit: a show, ostensibly crime and safety awareness, carrying the quality of something made by someone who knows exactly what they are constructing. You placed the voice on the third listen. Worked backward from the transmission source. Followed it as far as it would go this month, which was further than you had any right to expect.\nYou have a location now. Not where she sleeps — that remains ahead of you — but where she works, and something of how she moves. It is enough to continue from.\n\n### Brandy Old Fashioned\nShe is harder to find than expected.\nThree weeks of careful enquiries through the right channels and she never resolves into anything solid — no haven, no pattern, no address. Then: a name, attached to a description, attached to a circuit of fundraisers and gallery openings she has apparently been working with considerable purpose. The people who mention her do so with the particular warmth of those who have been charmed recently. She is visible in certain rooms. You have not been in those rooms. You know she exists in them.\nIt is a beginning. She is someone who knows how to be present without being knowable, and you have enough respect for that to proceed carefully.\n\n### Mister Cellophane\nObfuscate is the logical extension of everything you already do. You have spent decades learning how to be unremarkable, how to occupy a room without registering in it, how to ask questions in ways that do not feel like questions. This is simply that, made permanent.\nSeeing your grandsire again reminded you that not all threats announce themselves, and some things are better faced invisible.\n\n## Merit Actions\n### Action 1\nThe contact takes three days to respond. When he does, it is careful.\n\n## Touchstone\nYou know Elise's route now. You tell yourself this is because you are a careful man who observes carefully, which is true, but it is not why you are here.\nElise stops to look at something in a shop window and the light catches the angle of her jaw and your chest does the thing it has been doing since you first saw her, a kind of seizing that should not be possible in something without a heartbeat. Her name is not Astrid. You know her name is not Astrid. You have been telling yourself this for six months and it has not helped at all.\nElise turns the key in her door and goes inside and the light comes on and you walk away before you do something you cannot take back.\n\n## Letter\nDear Conrad,\n\nPrimogen. Yes. I read your letter twice to be certain I had understood correctly.\n\nI will not pretend I did not expect the Sheriff's office to be yours. You expected it too, which is why you have written to me in the language of acceptance rather than the language of satisfaction. I know the difference. I have been reading your letters for a very long time.\n\nThe question I would put to you is not whether you will honour the position (of course you will; you are incapable of doing otherwise) but whether you will allow yourself to want what is actually in front of you, rather than mourning what is not. Primogen is not nothing. In a city this new, it may be everything.\n\nGod's plans and ours rarely align on the first attempt. This is not news to either of us.\n\nYour affectionate mentor,\nDr Flanders\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Dockyard\nThere is something wrong with the animals this month.\nYou notice it on the first night — a particular quality of restlessness in the creatures near the waterfront, a tension that runs through them like a current. By the third week the docks themselves are disrupted. Workers complaining at shift change, operations running short, an energy in the air that makes people move faster and speak less. The blood here is thin; you leave each feeding with less than you came for, which is not new for this territory, but the degree of it is.\nYou are not the only one working these streets, and this month that has been unusually visible. Two figures, over several nights — Doc, who walks like she owns the ground she is standing on, and Macheath, who watches everything she cannot. They made no attempt at concealment. The opposite, in fact. Whatever they were doing in the Dockyard, they wanted it noticed.\nCarthians. You know the type.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18195:        "outcome_text": "## Feeding\nSubtle — seduction and willing vessels; you draw people to you and feed when they arrive\nManipulation + Empathy — 5 dice\nThe Academy, The Dockyard — The Academy — +3\n\n## Projects\n### What Do We Know About Eve\nEve Lockridge is Premier and you know almost nothing about her. You spend the month changing that.\nLHL Transport is a real company — ASIC registration, legitimate freight operations, Torrens title, company directors on record. Eve's public persona is polished and controlled. The mortal infrastructure is clean at the surface level, but you get a sense that with a little more digging there might be more than meets the eye.\n\n### Territory Watch\nYou walk your primary feeding grounds carefully, reading them with the attention you give to anything that matters.\nThe Dockyard is occupied. Kirk Grimm is working the territory with the quiet diligence of someone running a patrol route. Doc Kane and Macheath are also visible — deliberately so, the kind of conspicuous presence that is a statement. The infestation is worse than you first thought, concentrated near the shipping containers in a pattern that is not natural.\nThe Academy has the particular quality of contested ground. Multiple Kindred operating here, not all of them careful. You note the pattern without closing the distance.\n\n### Library Occult\nYou spend time building a reference collection in your area of primary interest.\n\n### Where Does Carver Sleep\nYou want to know where Carver goes to ground.\nYou narrow the range to the Dockyard precinct and identify a pattern in his movement. You do not have an address yet.\n\n## Merit Actions\n### Action 1\nWord comes back that LHL Transport has threads running into the Dockyard's freight infrastructure, and those threads are not clean. The company has contacts in the dockside underworld: the kind of contacts that facilitate movement of things that do not appear on manifests. This is not a company that wandered into this space accidentally.\n\n### Action 6\nconsecration.\n\n## Touchstone\nHis name was Marco. It lasted six weeks and it was a disaster from the beginning in the way that the best things sometimes are, and then it was over, and you have not stopped thinking about it since.\nNot about him exactly. About what it felt like. You had forgotten that you could want something that urgently, that you could be that present in your own body, that the hours could disappear that way. Six weeks of feeling completely alive and then it ended and you went back to being what you are, and the contrast has been sitting in you like a splinter ever since.\nYou drive past the bar where you met him. You do not go in.\nST Note:  Marco was invented to fill a gap. Ludica's submission lists a previous lover as her touchstone without further detail. Interpreted as a recent, brief affair in Sydney to keep the touchstone present and active. If Sky has someone more specific in mind we will replace this.\n\n## Letter\nDear Diary,\n\nMy first court in Sydney. Understanding the politics and vampires of Sydney has been a new experience. I have to say these vampires have been really interesting individuals so far. I do look forward to speaking to more of them, especially in the upcoming court proceedings. With Sydney having no structures for vampire society, it is concerning to me. To remain myself, I think there can be something new here even as a traditionalist. There definitely can be something different to make into. Shall see how things plan out and continue to seek more information.\nST Note:  Ludica wrote to no one. The entry stands alone.\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Academy\nYou move through the Academy with purpose, reading it the way you have learned to read territories — the flow of people, the points of friction, the places where the air has a different quality. The student population has an unusual quality this month, a social warmth that does not quite map to season or circumstance. Something is running through it. You note it and move on.\nOne night mid-month the rain came in wrong. Not the rain itself — the smell of it, the pressure of it, something underneath the weather that did not belong to weather. Mortals pulled off the streets without knowing why, animals in the precincts refusing to settle, the particular edge in the air of something large and hungry moving through. Your blood felt it before your mind did. Whatever it was, it passed by morning.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18240:      "published_outcome": "## Feeding\nSubtle — seduction and willing vessels; you draw people to you and feed when they arrive\nManipulation + Empathy — 5 dice\nThe Academy, The Dockyard — The Academy — +3\n\n## Projects\n### What Do We Know About Eve\nEve Lockridge is Premier and you know almost nothing about her. You spend the month changing that.\nLHL Transport is a real company — ASIC registration, legitimate freight operations, Torrens title, company directors on record. Eve's public persona is polished and controlled. The mortal infrastructure is clean at the surface level, but you get a sense that with a little more digging there might be more than meets the eye.\n\n### Territory Watch\nYou walk your primary feeding grounds carefully, reading them with the attention you give to anything that matters.\nThe Dockyard is occupied. Kirk Grimm is working the territory with the quiet diligence of someone running a patrol route. Doc Kane and Macheath are also visible — deliberately so, the kind of conspicuous presence that is a statement. The infestation is worse than you first thought, concentrated near the shipping containers in a pattern that is not natural.\nThe Academy has the particular quality of contested ground. Multiple Kindred operating here, not all of them careful. You note the pattern without closing the distance.\n\n### Library Occult\nYou spend time building a reference collection in your area of primary interest.\n\n### Where Does Carver Sleep\nYou want to know where Carver goes to ground.\nYou narrow the range to the Dockyard precinct and identify a pattern in his movement. You do not have an address yet.\n\n## Merit Actions\n### Action 1\nWord comes back that LHL Transport has threads running into the Dockyard's freight infrastructure, and those threads are not clean. The company has contacts in the dockside underworld: the kind of contacts that facilitate movement of things that do not appear on manifests. This is not a company that wandered into this space accidentally.\n\n### Action 6\nconsecration.\n\n## Touchstone\nHis name was Marco. It lasted six weeks and it was a disaster from the beginning in the way that the best things sometimes are, and then it was over, and you have not stopped thinking about it since.\nNot about him exactly. About what it felt like. You had forgotten that you could want something that urgently, that you could be that present in your own body, that the hours could disappear that way. Six weeks of feeling completely alive and then it ended and you went back to being what you are, and the contrast has been sitting in you like a splinter ever since.\nYou drive past the bar where you met him. You do not go in.\nST Note:  Marco was invented to fill a gap. Ludica's submission lists a previous lover as her touchstone without further detail. Interpreted as a recent, brief affair in Sydney to keep the touchstone present and active. If Sky has someone more specific in mind we will replace this.\n\n## Letter\nDear Diary,\n\nMy first court in Sydney. Understanding the politics and vampires of Sydney has been a new experience. I have to say these vampires have been really interesting individuals so far. I do look forward to speaking to more of them, especially in the upcoming court proceedings. With Sydney having no structures for vampire society, it is concerning to me. To remain myself, I think there can be something new here even as a traditionalist. There definitely can be something different to make into. Shall see how things plan out and continue to seek more information.\nST Note:  Ludica wrote to no one. The entry stands alone.\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Academy\nYou move through the Academy with purpose, reading it the way you have learned to read territories — the flow of people, the points of friction, the places where the air has a different quality. The student population has an unusual quality this month, a social warmth that does not quite map to season or circumstance. Something is running through it. You note it and move on.\nOne night mid-month the rain came in wrong. Not the rain itself — the smell of it, the pressure of it, something underneath the weather that did not belong to weather. Mortals pulled off the streets without knowing why, animals in the precincts refusing to settle, the particular edge in the air of something large and hungry moving through. Your blood felt it before your mind did. Whatever it was, it passed by morning.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18380:        "outcome_text": "## Feeding\nCovert — identifies targets through observation, isolates them with Dominate, feeds and removes the memory\nIntelligence + Subterfuge + Dominate — 14 dice (Discipline in pool: Dramatic Failure on zero successes)\nThe Academy, The Harbour, The Second City, The North Shore — The Academy — +3 / The Second City — +2\n\n## Projects\n### Made Men\nYou spend time in the places where the criminal infrastructure of Sydney actually lives — not the police records version, not the news version, the real version. Dockside bars. Late-night logistics depots. The peripheral conversations of people who move things that do not appear on manifests. You listen.\nBy the end of the month you have the broad shape of how crime works in this city — who the players are, where the money moves, which operations are established and which are still finding their feet.\n\n### House Hunting\nThe property is in the upper North Shore — a converted warehouse with a private basement level, reinforced entry points, and the kind of architectural detail that suggests the previous owner also had things to protect. You have it refitted before the month is out, the security layered and professional, the address unattached to any of your operating names.\n\n### Good Help is Hard to Find\nThe target is selected with care — not loyalty, not initiative, malleability. Someone with enough capability to be useful and enough instability to be shaped. You find them through the professional circles that surround your business interests; a mid-level administrator with access to the right systems and a particular quality of quiet desperation.\nWhat you put in place is thorough. They will carry nothing that points back to you.\n\n### It's Not Shampoo\nConditioning Devotion is not something you pick up quickly. The theory is sound — long-term compulsion seeded below the threshold of Dominate's normal reach — but the practice requires a specific kind of patience that you are still developing.\nYou work through the theoretical construction this downtime. The framework is taking shape.\n\n## Touchstone\nYou have been watching him for three weeks before you introduce yourself. He is exactly what you were looking for — mid-thirties, smart enough to be genuinely useful, hungry enough to make bad decisions without needing to be pushed. He runs a small investment advisory out of an office in Barangaroo that does marginally better than its peers because he works longer hours than anyone should.\nYou meet him at a function. You let him do most of the talking. He has a pitch ready for anyone who looks like money, and you look like money, so he gives it to you. It is not a bad pitch.\nWhat you find yourself doing, in the car afterwards, is remembering a version of yourself that would have delivered almost exactly the same pitch. The same confidence. The same slightly-too-fast delivery that gives away how much he wants it to land.\nYou do not need him for anything specific yet. You are keeping him close because watching him is doing something for you that you have not entirely worked out.\nST Note:  Reed's primary touchstone is a Sydney business contact — ambitious, corruptible, pre-consciously reminiscent of Reed's mortal self. Conan to supply a name. Does not know Reed is Kindred.\n\n## Letter\nReed,\n\nSydney sounds promising. The speed of your consolidation is noted and appreciated — you were always efficient when the opportunity was genuine rather than manufactured.\n\nA word of caution on the premier. A fledgling holding Praxis in a city this size suggests either extraordinary circumstance or extraordinary backing. Probably both. Do not be so focused on what she is doing that you miss who put her there. The Carthians rarely produce leaders of their own; they tend to inherit them from other covenants or have them installed from outside. Find the original transaction.\n\nThe Invictus presence you describe concerns me less than its absence elsewhere. If the First Estate is thin on the ground in a new court, someone made a decision about that. Find out whose decision it was.\n\nKeep the finance work clean. I will be watching the Sydney exposure.\n\nAbigail\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Harbour is where the money moves and where the people who follow money spend their time. You move through it with purpose and without noise — the kind of presence that registers as belonging.\nThe blood is thin this month. Too many feeders, not enough room. You take what you need.\nOne night the harbour went strange. The rain carried something — a hunger in the air, a taint that animals registered before any mortal could. Gulls off the water, dock rats scattering, working dogs straining at their chains. The vitae you drew that night had an edge to it. Whatever passed through the Harbour was not a natural storm.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18425:      "published_outcome": "## Feeding\nCovert — identifies targets through observation, isolates them with Dominate, feeds and removes the memory\nIntelligence + Subterfuge + Dominate — 14 dice (Discipline in pool: Dramatic Failure on zero successes)\nThe Academy, The Harbour, The Second City, The North Shore — The Academy — +3 / The Second City — +2\n\n## Projects\n### Made Men\nYou spend time in the places where the criminal infrastructure of Sydney actually lives — not the police records version, not the news version, the real version. Dockside bars. Late-night logistics depots. The peripheral conversations of people who move things that do not appear on manifests. You listen.\nBy the end of the month you have the broad shape of how crime works in this city — who the players are, where the money moves, which operations are established and which are still finding their feet.\n\n### House Hunting\nThe property is in the upper North Shore — a converted warehouse with a private basement level, reinforced entry points, and the kind of architectural detail that suggests the previous owner also had things to protect. You have it refitted before the month is out, the security layered and professional, the address unattached to any of your operating names.\n\n### Good Help is Hard to Find\nThe target is selected with care — not loyalty, not initiative, malleability. Someone with enough capability to be useful and enough instability to be shaped. You find them through the professional circles that surround your business interests; a mid-level administrator with access to the right systems and a particular quality of quiet desperation.\nWhat you put in place is thorough. They will carry nothing that points back to you.\n\n### It's Not Shampoo\nConditioning Devotion is not something you pick up quickly. The theory is sound — long-term compulsion seeded below the threshold of Dominate's normal reach — but the practice requires a specific kind of patience that you are still developing.\nYou work through the theoretical construction this downtime. The framework is taking shape.\n\n## Touchstone\nYou have been watching him for three weeks before you introduce yourself. He is exactly what you were looking for — mid-thirties, smart enough to be genuinely useful, hungry enough to make bad decisions without needing to be pushed. He runs a small investment advisory out of an office in Barangaroo that does marginally better than its peers because he works longer hours than anyone should.\nYou meet him at a function. You let him do most of the talking. He has a pitch ready for anyone who looks like money, and you look like money, so he gives it to you. It is not a bad pitch.\nWhat you find yourself doing, in the car afterwards, is remembering a version of yourself that would have delivered almost exactly the same pitch. The same confidence. The same slightly-too-fast delivery that gives away how much he wants it to land.\nYou do not need him for anything specific yet. You are keeping him close because watching him is doing something for you that you have not entirely worked out.\nST Note:  Reed's primary touchstone is a Sydney business contact — ambitious, corruptible, pre-consciously reminiscent of Reed's mortal self. Conan to supply a name. Does not know Reed is Kindred.\n\n## Letter\nReed,\n\nSydney sounds promising. The speed of your consolidation is noted and appreciated — you were always efficient when the opportunity was genuine rather than manufactured.\n\nA word of caution on the premier. A fledgling holding Praxis in a city this size suggests either extraordinary circumstance or extraordinary backing. Probably both. Do not be so focused on what she is doing that you miss who put her there. The Carthians rarely produce leaders of their own; they tend to inherit them from other covenants or have them installed from outside. Find the original transaction.\n\nThe Invictus presence you describe concerns me less than its absence elsewhere. If the First Estate is thin on the ground in a new court, someone made a decision about that. Find out whose decision it was.\n\nKeep the finance work clean. I will be watching the Sydney exposure.\n\nAbigail\n\n## Territory Reports\n### The Harbour is where the money moves and where the people who follow money spend their time. You move through it with purpose and without noise — the kind of presence that registers as belonging.\nThe blood is thin this month. Too many feeders, not enough room. You take what you need.\nOne night the harbour went strange. The rain carried something — a hunger in the air, a taint that animals registered before any mortal could. Gulls off the water, dock rats scattering, working dogs straining at their chains. The vitae you drew that night had an edge to it. Whatever passed through the Harbour was not a natural storm.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18471:            "pool_player": "Intelligence + Streetwise (Rumours speciality, 9-Again) — 6 dice  |  Rolls: [7, 1, 8, 4, 3, 5]  |  Result: 1 success",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18472:            "pool_validated": "Intelligence + Streetwise (Rumours speciality, 9-Again) — 6 dice  |  Rolls: [7, 1, 8, 4, 3, 5]  |  Result: 1 success",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18705:        "travel": "I walk from the nearest train station. Under \"Face in the Crowd\". No special precautions. If anyone gets too close a flash of Dread Presence normally get them looking at their feet. There is no ruse entourage this time. No one noticed last time.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18761:        "project_1_description": "This is done by not using my Contacts (Underworld) for information gathering this DT. Instead, they are pushing info out through the \"Wet-Interrogator\" aligned channels, as I will pick up \"kindred\" associated work - something easy and lightweight to touch the network rather than overtly announce our presence!. That is to say, there are those amongst the great unwashed who some wealthy clients pay to have discretely extracted. If Xavier also maintains his PT this DT we will likely then take a 'Carthian' job together - to \"catch and release\" a trouble-maker. Our specialty!",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:18997:        "outcome_text": "## Story Moment\n\nY,\nne[X]t time, sp[A]re me the postage.\n[V]ery little here w[I]ll surprise you.\nth[E] [R]ain stopped on Tuesday.\n[USE]. Strange as ever.\n\n## Territory Pulse — The North Shore\n\nThe North Shore is well looked after this cycle and the blood comes accordingly. It runs warm and steady, drawn from bodies that are getting their sleep and eating well, and the territory carries a settled, well-kept feel. There are enough of you working the grounds that you notice the others passing through, but not so many that the kine show the marks of it.\n\nSomething strange threads through the streets all the same. Long shadows fall where they should not, things turn up at the edge of vision and are gone when looked at directly, keys and wallets and small possessions go missing in greater numbers than they ought. People speak of feeling alone in busy rooms and getting lost on streets they have walked for years. Underneath that, something looser and more primal, the kind of nights that run later than intended and leave a faint corruption on the morning.\n\nAcross this month, there was modest Circle of the Crone effort in the territory, with a light Carthian counter-effort pulling against it. No single hand stood out clearly enough to be known for certain. In the centre of it, Anichka was constantly seen doing the good work, blessings given by hand and small mercies done in person.\n\n## Project 1\n\nYou push the work out through the Wet-Interrogator channels rather than through your Underworld lines this month. The job that comes back is a catch-and-release on one of the Great Unwashed, the kind your specialty was built for. The work is light enough to keep your hand in and quiet enough not to announce you. The Great Unwashed do not yet know your name. They will know there is someone, and the someone is not Ballsack.\n\n## Keeping the Keeper\n\nYou arrive at the haven on the night the spike goes in, and you stay for nine. Keeper hangs on the tree. Keeper warned you, but he did not tell you the shape of what was to come. The shape, when it arrives, is this; he is beyond the edge of a frenzy that is not the ordinary kind, the kind a Kindred falls into and recovers from, but the kind that does not end, the kind that goes all the way through and out the other side. He does not fall. He does not recover. He hangs at there for nine nights, and the frenzy is beyond even that which the Nightmare in your blood can summon, and you feel its edge through the line he has run into you. Water and vitae run from his body pooling around the branch. The pool grows. The frenzy comes off him in waves and you take some of it second-hand through the tie that should not be there, and you hold what you take. You stand guard not truly knowing they depth of why and the only visitors are Ivana who drains a white owl into Keepers screaming mouth each night and Anichka who comes and sings to him countless songs. Charlie is rarely there, but when he is there is a persistent glower, the racon of a man whose home has been threated and had no choice in the matter. The cover holds around you both. Charlie does not let you spread your blood for the creation of an Oubliette, but you find no need to use your powers. The time is long and the incessant screaming of the beast does nothing to make the time pass quicker. You feel you have been through a tribulation yourself, passing the nights watching as roots and vines move of their own accord to lap at the ever-growing pool of blood. On the ninth night Keeper comes back into himself enough to know who has been beside him. What you see on his return is the void made manifest, the gaping maw of creation and destruction poured into an undead vessel. The branch comes to life and snakes out of him, bowing in supplication before crumpling to dust. You look in his eyes and know you could ask any question and receive truth from his mouth, but in the receiving you would know the void in a way that way drive you towards destruction. Keeper is safe and he owes you a favour. The favour is large. He knows it. So do you. You walk out of the haven with the picture intact and the location not. The route does not stay with you. The street does not stay with you. By the time you have reached your own door you could not return to the house if you tried. The Crone keeps that for itself.\n\n## The Old Ways\n\nYou spend the month with worm-form in the deep places under the necropolis you have already claimed. The maps you have are the maps anyone has. The doors you push through are the ones not on any map. You find what you came to find on the seventeenth night, behind a grate that has not been lifted in eighty years: a chamber dug by hands you recognise as Nosferatu hands, the marks of older Kindred craftsmen on the walls, alcoves built for purposes you can name, and at the far end a passage that goes further down than your night's work would let you follow. The builders were here. They left more than you have yet seen. In a quiet moment you swear you are being watched, you turn around quickly, your heart beating once, a rare thing, but in the turning you catch your hand on a jutting nail and a splash of blood arcs on to the stones, where it does not stay for long. As it seeps into the rock you feel the air stir, and a sudden increase in pressure, and the sense that something very old and very large has begun to awaken.\n\n## Project 4\n\nYou spend the month's time at the bench in your own haven. The Safe Place gains a layer of work in the doors and the approaches; you have closed two ways in that you had previously left open as conveniences. The Closed Book is the harder work. You sit with your own face in the mirror until the face stops giving anything away to the kind of person who would be reading it. The worm comes together at the end. What was preparation becomes a thing you can do, and the deep places under the city are open to you now in a way they were not a month ago.\n\nXP was not get spent on Mandragora Garden (Only Fucking Thief). Added True Worm and",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:19299:            "response": "You push the work out through the Wet-Interrogator channels rather than through your Underworld lines this month. The job that comes back is a catch-and-release on one of the Great Unwashed, the kind your specialty was built for. The work is light enough to keep your hand in and quiet enough not to announce you. The Great Unwashed do not yet know your name. They will know there is someone, and the someone is not Ballsack.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:21472:        "game_recount_2": "Argued with the \"Protector\" about their methods of investigating, especially with the threats levelled out about maintaining regencies",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:21611:        "game_recount": "1. Discovered Einar Solveig had an accident in the Harbour Regency\n\n2. Argued with the \"Protector\" about their methods of investigating, especially with the threats levelled out about maintaining regencies\n\n3. Took Etsy under my wing for tutelage, as ordered by Rene St Dominique",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:23082:        "project_1_description": "Jack spends time to check in with his Visitors (humans who maintain the surveillance web for the Room), praising those who have done well, chastising those who have not, using his Auspex to probe their minds to secure truthful compliance; and announces that he has a special challenge and reward for the most dedicated Visitor to motivate them (see DT 2).",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24352:        "outcome_text": "## Story Moment\n\nKyle is telling you about the wedding before you have sat down. He stands halfway up when you come in, points at the empty chair, and starts in the middle of a sentence about the suit his son had to be talked into.\nThe boy did the speech himself. Wrote it on the train to the venue. The bride's mother cried in the part about Kyle's late wife, which was the part Kyle had been worried about, and Kyle is telling you this in pieces, out of order, because the pieces are still moving inside him.\nYou ask the right questions in the right places. Kyle does not need you to. Kyle would have told this to the bartender. He would have told it to the wall. But you ask, and the answering makes him happier than he already was.\nAt one point Kyle says, quite simply, that you should have seen him. The boy. Standing up there. He says it as a man says the most important sentence he has the words for.\nYou have been alive for one hundred and eighty-two years. You have not made anyone. You have not stood in a room and watched something you put into the world choose its own life. You have not wanted to, and tonight you do not know whether the not-wanting was wisdom or a failure of nerve.\nKyle taps the table once and asks how you are. You tell him the boat is coming along. He listens with his whole attention, as he listens to everything you tell him, and you sit with the late warm hour of his life and find, tonight, that you are glad for him.\n\n## Territory Pulse — The Second City\n\nThe Second City is keeping itself together this cycle and the blood comes as expected. It runs ordinary and unremarkable, drawn from bodies that are neither thriving nor wearing down, and the territory carries the unfussed quality of a place that has been left to its own rhythms. There are enough of you working the grounds to know that others are passing through, but the kine themselves have not been overworked, and the take goes down clean.\n\nWalk the streets after dark and there is little to mark them out. Lights burn where lights ought to burn, the late venues keep their usual hours, and the people on the pavements move with the easy distraction of city life. Nothing has been done to lift the place this cycle and nothing has been done to pull it down. It is simply itself, holding the line of what it was.\n\n## Project 1\n\nPeople say your name in rooms you are not in. Some of them say it with the suspicion that attaches to older Kindred who have outlived more Movements than they have joined. Others say it with the respect of younger Carthians who have only ever read about people who were part of the fight before they were Embraced. Underneath both registers is the same chatter: that Sydney might just become the realisation of the great dream that is a Carthian city, held by and for Carthians, and that the conversation about whether such a thing is truly possible has begun to include you.\n\n## A Man About Town\n\nYou give Reed one night a week, and you give it visibly. You walk the docks with your senses open and let whoever is watching see a Ventrue at work. The list holds. Nobody is feeding here who is not on the paper Reed handed you, and Xavier's arrangement is the one you already knew about. You cross paths with Reed on a Tuesday and neither of you needs to say much. The Kine are easy. The teeth are accounted for. The Harbour is quiet, and it is quiet because it is working.\n\n## Project 3\n\nYou take the man behind the bottle-shop loading dock on a Tuesday night. He sees you coming and decides to make it interesting. You let him try for about four seconds before you stop letting him. You take what you need from his throat while he is still trying to work out which arm has stopped responding. You leave him propped against the bins. He will be found before morning. Whoever finds him will assume what people assume about men found near bottle-shop bins, and the assumption will not include you.\n\n## Following the French Woman\n\nYou have spent the better part of the month gliding above Rene, the watch is quiet but it suits you.\nOver time, you get used to tracking Rene by the colourful beret. Especially at night your eyes are sharp for a raven. \nThen one night you follow her, the evening is routine. You drop to a low branch close enough to read her at proper range and the creature before you has no predator taint upon her. \nShe is a mortal in a red beret who has never been Rene. Try as you might, you do not find Rene that night.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24564:            "response": "You have spent the better part of the month gliding above Rene, the watch is quiet but it suits you.\nOver time, you get used to tracking Rene by the colourful beret. Especially at night your eyes are sharp for a raven. \nThen one night you follow her, the evening is routine. You drop to a low branch close enough to read her at proper range and the creature before you has no predator taint upon her. \nShe is a mortal in a red beret who has never been Rene. Try as you might, you do not find Rene that night.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24707:        "feeding_description": "(Just letting you know that I can't unselect a discipline once selected- I've made a bug report about it- I'll use it this time but let's hope I don't get a failure, huh?)\n\nRene walks the venues of the second city, for those people drinking alone- for the dates that haven't shown up, for the people who need someone and don't really care who. Picking the best target with Auspex, she slips in like a sigh and asks them about their troubles. She listens, for a time, perhaps buys them a drink and offers to walk with them for some air... Eventually, in a secluded place, she'll bring them close and offer a shoulder to cry on before getting what she really needs- all the troubles they expounded discarded in favour of sweet vitae. \n\nAs they are regaining their wits, she makes a calm exit.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24731:        "project_1_xp_trait": "(I assume I can pick up Court Jester as it's a 2 dot merit that's not got any specific actions that are required, but I will be using an action to bump professional training. For the 3rd dot of professional training I'm going to be picking the new asset skill 'Larceny' with the specialties of 'Larceny: Pickpocketing' and 'Empathy: Motives', which I hope to explain in my IC reasoning. I've not actually got that many skills I can specialize in/make an asset, so I tried to pick some I thought appropriate.)\n\nI've got my footing on Sydney now, and though I've my hands full with the regency- I've time enough now to resume the work that still somewhat connects me to my past self. The process of constructing collective action can be undertaken in a myriad of ways- I knew some people back in England who would work closely with the companies they organized against to find an appropriate middle ground all could be happy with.\n\nI never worked like that- and since my indoctrination into these ruthless and bloody nights, I feel that was the correct choice; There can be no compromises- I will bring to bare the grievances of the worker and if so refused, will find other ways of getting my point across... even if that means pocketing the company-man's wallet and paying him a visit at his listed address during the small hours of the night. That's how you get change, by demonstrating the walls of process immaterial. \n\nTonight I'm meeting with some union men who have grown comfortable in the city that has until now been bereft of beasts in the night and puppet masters upon the stage. I of course will not let them know the true extent of their hopelessness, but I hope to get across some of the troubles to come- and offer myself as an apt consultant.\n\nI'll gauge their interest and put on a smile, no kindred powers needed. If they dismiss me? I'll do to them what I've done to so many company men, and take their info for a more private conversation.\n\n-\n\nConducting this business I can't help but think how absurd the machinations of court really are. It has been a musing of mine for a while, stuffing mad predators together in a room- all pretending to be moral and chivalrous before ripping each others throats out. I am expected to conduct a real-estate survey after being stabbed in the heart? It's enough to drive a woman to apathy. \n\nAnd so it has. It's obvious I have no touch for etiquette despite my heritage, so I won't pretend. I will face the court with something all the rarer- plain faced and indifferent honesty. Call me foolish if you wish, but at least I'm not pretending to be a knight.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24738:        "regency_action": "There's been much focus upon the scramble for Sydney over the past months- it is of course ongoing and will surely result in more death and violence, but I wish to highlight the lighter side to all of you whom have come from across the globe. We, united by our complete foreignness to this place, have a type of freedom never seen- especially here in 2C. It is an opportunity to be celebrated.\n\nThe mortals of Sydney are untouched by fear, innocent and fresh. This, of course, makes feeding easy- but I ask you all to consider that there is other nourishment we can gain from them. Nourishment of ideas, of art and musings. I ask you all to engage with them, and not to smother them out in dominative dismissal- we can use them, after all. Soon, court will be hosted in this wonderful territory of ours- and as the night approaches, I hope to see you all prove that we are growing into something distinct from the rest of the world from which we all came. Paint the alleys! Take the stage! Join a chorus! Fit into the space of untainted mortal expression and feed as you would from their veins!\n\nSoon, more Kine come- and with them, their ignorant and wonderful thoughts. We must take care with them.\n\nThey only live once, after all.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:24785:        "project_4_description": "Whatever Keeper is doing seems big- I know as much from the tremors of the cacophony last month. Given that he has also decided to link himself to me in some manner or another,  that might help in working out his movements and motives- especially if I pump some Auspex into it. \n\nIf I can identify any of- where it is happening, why it is happening, how it is happening, or what the fuck is happening, I'll take it is a win. Especially if it gives me any chance to brace for it.\n\nI have spoken a big game in my letter of reply- that the movement lives in me and thus is unquenchable... but to an extent, I fear- this elder seems something other than Kindred, and he has Charlie at his back. A very dour combination. Perhaps using my understanding of the compulsions of our kind, coupled with my experience of these city streets, I can resist this tyranny of ego and weather what is coming.\n\nI also suspect that Conrad may have received a similar letter- and will be on the lookout for the scrawny bastard. \n\nKeeper has warned me of final death if I'm to interrupt him during the process unannounced... so I won't be going alone. Taking Casmirir along should serve to bolster my chances and keep my beast from doing anything unfortunate if it is so badly effected by whatever Keeper has in store.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:25310:        "personal_story_text": "Carver asks James to take him somewhere that is special to him. Somewhere where James feels is a \"core memeory\".",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:30030:        "project_3_description": "On becoming aware of the existence of an old necropolis Xavier starts the search to find it. He reaches out through his various contacts (foreign and domestic) to look for clues to where it might have been. Searched information on subterranean areas across the history of the city (maps, plans, geological surveys). looking for unusual gaps to information about it being accessed (especially old areas that had been more recently accessed during the time vampires were absent from the city). Looking for folklore about usual events linked to these subterranean sites and immediate surrounds.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:31409:          "outcome_summary": "You get wind of a special deceased estate auction of a person who is reputed to be a bon fide soothsayer. You wonder how credible it is, Vaucluse is not known for mystics."
server\scripts\archive\_backups\submission-territory-migration-2026-05-24T01-43-53-619Z.json:32903:              "text": "It's all good in the hood, especially the parties.",
