server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:4747:          "ic_correspondence": "Lord X (Sire to Premier Evangeline)\n\nThe Kindred of the City are settling into their new home. Your Childe appears to be acquitting herself well - establishing connections, making friends and... \"allies\".\nRegents have been selected, and territories established - I expect that the fairly amicable relationships between the Covenants may soon be tested once the Kindred begin to find themselves more comfortable, or less so.\nThough the shadow war that appears to be happening between the Crone and the Sanctum seems to have caused some anomalies that put pressure on the sanctity of the Masquerade - for now, your investments seem secure, and your Childe may yet earn my respect on her own merits before the expiry of the terms of our agreement.\n\n- E",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:4874:        "correspondence": "Lord X (Sire to Premier Evangeline)\n\nThe Kindred of the City are settling into their new home. Your Childe appears to be acquitting herself well - establishing connections, making friends and... \"allies\".\nRegents have been selected, and territories established - I expect that the fairly amicable relationships between the Covenants may soon be tested once the Kindred begin to find themselves more comfortable, or less so.\nThough the shadow war that appears to be happening between the Crone and the Sanctum seems to have caused some anomalies that put pressure on the sanctity of the Masquerade - for now, your investments seem secure, and your Childe may yet earn my respect on her own merits before the expiry of the terms of our agreement.\n\n- E",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:6272:          "casting": "Ritual Name/Level: Blood Witness L2\nCaster/s: Ivana\nTarget/s: Court Location - the Hub Theatre in Newtown\nDuration: 1 night. \nEffects and page reference: Smear Vitae on an area. Remotely observe through the spilled blood for one day per extra Vitae spent. (VTR: Coteries, p. 84 but put in pg 86 when you use the PDF. It is 1 dot ritual, but it is 2 dots on my sheet - probably because conversion things, I think, Symon?)\nVitae/Willpower Spent: 3\n\nIvana would like to arrive at the Court location before everyone else does, as discussed with the Crone, so she can set up 'security'. Charlie would likely be with her. Ivana would like to use 1 Vitae to smear some blood around the ballroom, in unobtrusive locations, like the underside of tables, or chairs (especially where PremiEve will sit), and she would rub some into any locks/padlocks/keyholes - logic being that if she is able to get some stuck in a nook or cranny, a little may remain, even if the rest is wiped away. Ivana would do the same in the 'private meeting space', again in the lock of the door and on the underside of a chair, and a smear on any external doorways, just in case. Happy for y'all to rejig this, if it feels too much - am going on the whole 'one location' thing, but 1 vitae per room. \n\nBe prepared for, \"Keeper, I'm hungry.\""
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:6317:        "sorcery_1_rite": "Ritual Name/Level: Blood Witness L2\nCaster/s: Ivana\nTarget/s: Court Location - the Hub Theatre in Newtown\nDuration: 1 night. \nEffects and page reference: Smear Vitae on an area. Remotely observe through the spilled blood for one day per extra Vitae spent. (VTR: Coteries, p. 84 but put in pg 86 when you use the PDF. It is 1 dot ritual, but it is 2 dots on my sheet - probably because conversion things, I think, Symon?)\nVitae/Willpower Spent: 3\n\nIvana would like to arrive at the Court location before everyone else does, as discussed with the Crone, so she can set up 'security'. Charlie would likely be with her. Ivana would like to use 1 Vitae to smear some blood around the ballroom, in unobtrusive locations, like the underside of tables, or chairs (especially where PremiEve will sit), and she would rub some into any locks/padlocks/keyholes - logic being that if she is able to get some stuck in a nook or cranny, a little may remain, even if the rest is wiped away. Ivana would do the same in the 'private meeting space', again in the lock of the door and on the underside of a chair, and a smear on any external doorways, just in case. Happy for y'all to rejig this, if it feels too much - am going on the whole 'one location' thing, but 1 vitae per room. \n\nBe prepared for, \"Keeper, I'm hungry.\"",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:6845:            "description": "Project Name: The Panopticon\nCharacters involved: Just me\nMerits & Bonuses: Trained Observer\nXP spend: n/a\nProject Description: \n\nJack has been tasked with securing the venue for Court on April 18th. He applies his skills as a director to surveil Court. \n\nThrough his High Society Allies, he negotiates permission from the owner (acquired for $25M in 2024) of a The Hub Theatre (shuttered and closed in 1996) on King Street in Newtown to allow him to put on a small exhibit for a dry run of a private viewing (Court), which he intends to repeat as an extended special exhibit during next DT for high society members (Moulding Room shenanigans). \n\n[full description of Court setup will be sent to STs] \nThe Exhibit consists of projectors with small screens and seats arranged around the art deco ballroom of the theatre profiling visual media over the past century of the Theatre's history -- vaudeville, silent movies, early black and white, colorised film, porn productions in the 70s/80s, and ultimately nothing from ~1996 onwards. The Final Exhibit shows a live feed, top down, of a camera with a LENSBABY Composer 2 Pro Bending Camera Lens mounted on the ceiling that shows the movement of Kindred around the ballroom, blurred focus around the edges by clear focus on the centre -- which is where the central seat for the Premier is located. [Primary dice pool to set up]\n\nWith his Eye Behind the Glass detournement active (on a camera in his Haven watching the feed from Court), Jack would be able to constantly keep an eye on that central spot of Court (who is talking to the Premier, and for how long) and gain some insights on the machinations of Court. [Secondary dice pool]",
