server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:10788:          "ic_correspondence": "Solidarity\n\nI've sent a list of names accompanying this missive, these are the Kindred important enough to attend court in Sydney. Territory is being divided, my fellow Carthians placing me in power over one of them for the moment- 'The Second city'. The cycle of Kindred dominance is spinning up. The silver lining at least, is that our fledgling Premier seemingly wants to do something all-together unique with the city. Obviously this is extremely confidential, but I'm an Anti-Obstructionist first, and a Carthian second. \n\nHer plan: To institute a rule- though both Carthian Law and practical enforcement, to preclude all but the least blood-potent kindred entrance into the city. \n\nOn one hand, this would bar those with extreme powers of the blood and the appetites that accompany them. On the other, it does encourage kindred to lean more heavily on their more mortal-facing powers. Then again, less potency means less blood to influence mortals with. I'm undecided about this, but probably have more pertinent issues to navigate.\n\nI've set up some roots in addition to the new territory, a public radio station and some informants in mortal affairs- though I worry many of the institutions of the city have been taken solidly by kindred, especially in the finance sector. I've also spoken more with the Crone member known as 'Alice Vunder'. They have a rather Anti-Obstructionist viewpoint. We've reached an understanding, and perhaps with a bit of a push, I can make a radical out of her. Then again, you never know with witches. \n\nI am, as ever, surrounded by cut-throat predators. I feel somewhat like a seagull in a hurricane.\n\nCest la vie. Mieux vaut être chanceux que bon.\n\n~R",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:10939:        "correspondence": "Solidarity\n\nI've sent a list of names accompanying this missive, these are the Kindred important enough to attend court in Sydney. Territory is being divided, my fellow Carthians placing me in power over one of them for the moment- 'The Second city'. The cycle of Kindred dominance is spinning up. The silver lining at least, is that our fledgling Premier seemingly wants to do something all-together unique with the city. Obviously this is extremely confidential, but I'm an Anti-Obstructionist first, and a Carthian second. \n\nHer plan: To institute a rule- though both Carthian Law and practical enforcement, to preclude all but the least blood-potent kindred entrance into the city. \n\nOn one hand, this would bar those with extreme powers of the blood and the appetites that accompany them. On the other, it does encourage kindred to lean more heavily on their more mortal-facing powers. Then again, less potency means less blood to influence mortals with. I'm undecided about this, but probably have more pertinent issues to navigate.\n\nI've set up some roots in addition to the new territory, a public radio station and some informants in mortal affairs- though I worry many of the institutions of the city have been taken solidly by kindred, especially in the finance sector. I've also spoken more with the Crone member known as 'Alice Vunder'. They have a rather Anti-Obstructionist viewpoint. We've reached an understanding, and perhaps with a bit of a push, I can make a radical out of her. Then again, you never know with witches. \n\nI am, as ever, surrounded by cut-throat predators. I feel somewhat like a seagull in a hurricane.\n\nCest la vie. Mieux vaut être chanceux que bon.\n\n~R",
