server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:18705:        "travel": "I walk from the nearest train station. Under \"Face in the Crowd\". No special precautions. If anyone gets too close a flash of Dread Presence normally get them looking at their feet. There is no ruse entourage this time. No one noticed last time.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:18761:        "project_1_description": "This is done by not using my Contacts (Underworld) for information gathering this DT. Instead, they are pushing info out through the \"Wet-Interrogator\" aligned channels, as I will pick up \"kindred\" associated work - something easy and lightweight to touch the network rather than overtly announce our presence!. That is to say, there are those amongst the great unwashed who some wealthy clients pay to have discretely extracted. If Xavier also maintains his PT this DT we will likely then take a 'Carthian' job together - to \"catch and release\" a trouble-maker. Our specialty!",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:18997:        "outcome_text": "## Story Moment\n\nY,\nne[X]t time, sp[A]re me the postage.\n[V]ery little here w[I]ll surprise you.\nth[E] [R]ain stopped on Tuesday.\n[USE]. Strange as ever.\n\n## Territory Pulse — The North Shore\n\nThe North Shore is well looked after this cycle and the blood comes accordingly. It runs warm and steady, drawn from bodies that are getting their sleep and eating well, and the territory carries a settled, well-kept feel. There are enough of you working the grounds that you notice the others passing through, but not so many that the kine show the marks of it.\n\nSomething strange threads through the streets all the same. Long shadows fall where they should not, things turn up at the edge of vision and are gone when looked at directly, keys and wallets and small possessions go missing in greater numbers than they ought. People speak of feeling alone in busy rooms and getting lost on streets they have walked for years. Underneath that, something looser and more primal, the kind of nights that run later than intended and leave a faint corruption on the morning.\n\nAcross this month, there was modest Circle of the Crone effort in the territory, with a light Carthian counter-effort pulling against it. No single hand stood out clearly enough to be known for certain. In the centre of it, Anichka was constantly seen doing the good work, blessings given by hand and small mercies done in person.\n\n## Project 1\n\nYou push the work out through the Wet-Interrogator channels rather than through your Underworld lines this month. The job that comes back is a catch-and-release on one of the Great Unwashed, the kind your specialty was built for. The work is light enough to keep your hand in and quiet enough not to announce you. The Great Unwashed do not yet know your name. They will know there is someone, and the someone is not Ballsack.\n\n## Keeping the Keeper\n\nYou arrive at the haven on the night the spike goes in, and you stay for nine. Keeper hangs on the tree. Keeper warned you, but he did not tell you the shape of what was to come. The shape, when it arrives, is this; he is beyond the edge of a frenzy that is not the ordinary kind, the kind a Kindred falls into and recovers from, but the kind that does not end, the kind that goes all the way through and out the other side. He does not fall. He does not recover. He hangs at there for nine nights, and the frenzy is beyond even that which the Nightmare in your blood can summon, and you feel its edge through the line he has run into you. Water and vitae run from his body pooling around the branch. The pool grows. The frenzy comes off him in waves and you take some of it second-hand through the tie that should not be there, and you hold what you take. You stand guard not truly knowing they depth of why and the only visitors are Ivana who drains a white owl into Keepers screaming mouth each night and Anichka who comes and sings to him countless songs. Charlie is rarely there, but when he is there is a persistent glower, the racon of a man whose home has been threated and had no choice in the matter. The cover holds around you both. Charlie does not let you spread your blood for the creation of an Oubliette, but you find no need to use your powers. The time is long and the incessant screaming of the beast does nothing to make the time pass quicker. You feel you have been through a tribulation yourself, passing the nights watching as roots and vines move of their own accord to lap at the ever-growing pool of blood. On the ninth night Keeper comes back into himself enough to know who has been beside him. What you see on his return is the void made manifest, the gaping maw of creation and destruction poured into an undead vessel. The branch comes to life and snakes out of him, bowing in supplication before crumpling to dust. You look in his eyes and know you could ask any question and receive truth from his mouth, but in the receiving you would know the void in a way that way drive you towards destruction. Keeper is safe and he owes you a favour. The favour is large. He knows it. So do you. You walk out of the haven with the picture intact and the location not. The route does not stay with you. The street does not stay with you. By the time you have reached your own door you could not return to the house if you tried. The Crone keeps that for itself.\n\n## The Old Ways\n\nYou spend the month with worm-form in the deep places under the necropolis you have already claimed. The maps you have are the maps anyone has. The doors you push through are the ones not on any map. You find what you came to find on the seventeenth night, behind a grate that has not been lifted in eighty years: a chamber dug by hands you recognise as Nosferatu hands, the marks of older Kindred craftsmen on the walls, alcoves built for purposes you can name, and at the far end a passage that goes further down than your night's work would let you follow. The builders were here. They left more than you have yet seen. In a quiet moment you swear you are being watched, you turn around quickly, your heart beating once, a rare thing, but in the turning you catch your hand on a jutting nail and a splash of blood arcs on to the stones, where it does not stay for long. As it seeps into the rock you feel the air stir, and a sudden increase in pressure, and the sense that something very old and very large has begun to awaken.\n\n## Project 4\n\nYou spend the month's time at the bench in your own haven. The Safe Place gains a layer of work in the doors and the approaches; you have closed two ways in that you had previously left open as conveniences. The Closed Book is the harder work. You sit with your own face in the mirror until the face stops giving anything away to the kind of person who would be reading it. The worm comes together at the end. What was preparation becomes a thing you can do, and the deep places under the city are open to you now in a way they were not a month ago.\n\nXP was not get spent on Mandragora Garden (Only Fucking Thief). Added True Worm and",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:19299:            "response": "You push the work out through the Wet-Interrogator channels rather than through your Underworld lines this month. The job that comes back is a catch-and-release on one of the Great Unwashed, the kind your specialty was built for. The work is light enough to keep your hand in and quiet enough not to announce you. The Great Unwashed do not yet know your name. They will know there is someone, and the someone is not Ballsack.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:21472:        "game_recount_2": "Argued with the \"Protector\" about their methods of investigating, especially with the threats levelled out about maintaining regencies",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:21611:        "game_recount": "1. Discovered Einar Solveig had an accident in the Harbour Regency\n\n2. Argued with the \"Protector\" about their methods of investigating, especially with the threats levelled out about maintaining regencies\n\n3. Took Etsy under my wing for tutelage, as ordered by Rene St Dominique",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:23082:        "project_1_description": "Jack spends time to check in with his Visitors (humans who maintain the surveillance web for the Room), praising those who have done well, chastising those who have not, using his Auspex to probe their minds to secure truthful compliance; and announces that he has a special challenge and reward for the most dedicated Visitor to motivate them (see DT 2).",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24352:        "outcome_text": "## Story Moment\n\nKyle is telling you about the wedding before you have sat down. He stands halfway up when you come in, points at the empty chair, and starts in the middle of a sentence about the suit his son had to be talked into.\nThe boy did the speech himself. Wrote it on the train to the venue. The bride's mother cried in the part about Kyle's late wife, which was the part Kyle had been worried about, and Kyle is telling you this in pieces, out of order, because the pieces are still moving inside him.\nYou ask the right questions in the right places. Kyle does not need you to. Kyle would have told this to the bartender. He would have told it to the wall. But you ask, and the answering makes him happier than he already was.\nAt one point Kyle says, quite simply, that you should have seen him. The boy. Standing up there. He says it as a man says the most important sentence he has the words for.\nYou have been alive for one hundred and eighty-two years. You have not made anyone. You have not stood in a room and watched something you put into the world choose its own life. You have not wanted to, and tonight you do not know whether the not-wanting was wisdom or a failure of nerve.\nKyle taps the table once and asks how you are. You tell him the boat is coming along. He listens with his whole attention, as he listens to everything you tell him, and you sit with the late warm hour of his life and find, tonight, that you are glad for him.\n\n## Territory Pulse — The Second City\n\nThe Second City is keeping itself together this cycle and the blood comes as expected. It runs ordinary and unremarkable, drawn from bodies that are neither thriving nor wearing down, and the territory carries the unfussed quality of a place that has been left to its own rhythms. There are enough of you working the grounds to know that others are passing through, but the kine themselves have not been overworked, and the take goes down clean.\n\nWalk the streets after dark and there is little to mark them out. Lights burn where lights ought to burn, the late venues keep their usual hours, and the people on the pavements move with the easy distraction of city life. Nothing has been done to lift the place this cycle and nothing has been done to pull it down. It is simply itself, holding the line of what it was.\n\n## Project 1\n\nPeople say your name in rooms you are not in. Some of them say it with the suspicion that attaches to older Kindred who have outlived more Movements than they have joined. Others say it with the respect of younger Carthians who have only ever read about people who were part of the fight before they were Embraced. Underneath both registers is the same chatter: that Sydney might just become the realisation of the great dream that is a Carthian city, held by and for Carthians, and that the conversation about whether such a thing is truly possible has begun to include you.\n\n## A Man About Town\n\nYou give Reed one night a week, and you give it visibly. You walk the docks with your senses open and let whoever is watching see a Ventrue at work. The list holds. Nobody is feeding here who is not on the paper Reed handed you, and Xavier's arrangement is the one you already knew about. You cross paths with Reed on a Tuesday and neither of you needs to say much. The Kine are easy. The teeth are accounted for. The Harbour is quiet, and it is quiet because it is working.\n\n## Project 3\n\nYou take the man behind the bottle-shop loading dock on a Tuesday night. He sees you coming and decides to make it interesting. You let him try for about four seconds before you stop letting him. You take what you need from his throat while he is still trying to work out which arm has stopped responding. You leave him propped against the bins. He will be found before morning. Whoever finds him will assume what people assume about men found near bottle-shop bins, and the assumption will not include you.\n\n## Following the French Woman\n\nYou have spent the better part of the month gliding above Rene, the watch is quiet but it suits you.\nOver time, you get used to tracking Rene by the colourful beret. Especially at night your eyes are sharp for a raven. \nThen one night you follow her, the evening is routine. You drop to a low branch close enough to read her at proper range and the creature before you has no predator taint upon her. \nShe is a mortal in a red beret who has never been Rene. Try as you might, you do not find Rene that night.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24564:            "response": "You have spent the better part of the month gliding above Rene, the watch is quiet but it suits you.\nOver time, you get used to tracking Rene by the colourful beret. Especially at night your eyes are sharp for a raven. \nThen one night you follow her, the evening is routine. You drop to a low branch close enough to read her at proper range and the creature before you has no predator taint upon her. \nShe is a mortal in a red beret who has never been Rene. Try as you might, you do not find Rene that night.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24707:        "feeding_description": "(Just letting you know that I can't unselect a discipline once selected- I've made a bug report about it- I'll use it this time but let's hope I don't get a failure, huh?)\n\nRene walks the venues of the second city, for those people drinking alone- for the dates that haven't shown up, for the people who need someone and don't really care who. Picking the best target with Auspex, she slips in like a sigh and asks them about their troubles. She listens, for a time, perhaps buys them a drink and offers to walk with them for some air... Eventually, in a secluded place, she'll bring them close and offer a shoulder to cry on before getting what she really needs- all the troubles they expounded discarded in favour of sweet vitae. \n\nAs they are regaining their wits, she makes a calm exit.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24731:        "project_1_xp_trait": "(I assume I can pick up Court Jester as it's a 2 dot merit that's not got any specific actions that are required, but I will be using an action to bump professional training. For the 3rd dot of professional training I'm going to be picking the new asset skill 'Larceny' with the specialties of 'Larceny: Pickpocketing' and 'Empathy: Motives', which I hope to explain in my IC reasoning. I've not actually got that many skills I can specialize in/make an asset, so I tried to pick some I thought appropriate.)\n\nI've got my footing on Sydney now, and though I've my hands full with the regency- I've time enough now to resume the work that still somewhat connects me to my past self. The process of constructing collective action can be undertaken in a myriad of ways- I knew some people back in England who would work closely with the companies they organized against to find an appropriate middle ground all could be happy with.\n\nI never worked like that- and since my indoctrination into these ruthless and bloody nights, I feel that was the correct choice; There can be no compromises- I will bring to bare the grievances of the worker and if so refused, will find other ways of getting my point across... even if that means pocketing the company-man's wallet and paying him a visit at his listed address during the small hours of the night. That's how you get change, by demonstrating the walls of process immaterial. \n\nTonight I'm meeting with some union men who have grown comfortable in the city that has until now been bereft of beasts in the night and puppet masters upon the stage. I of course will not let them know the true extent of their hopelessness, but I hope to get across some of the troubles to come- and offer myself as an apt consultant.\n\nI'll gauge their interest and put on a smile, no kindred powers needed. If they dismiss me? I'll do to them what I've done to so many company men, and take their info for a more private conversation.\n\n-\n\nConducting this business I can't help but think how absurd the machinations of court really are. It has been a musing of mine for a while, stuffing mad predators together in a room- all pretending to be moral and chivalrous before ripping each others throats out. I am expected to conduct a real-estate survey after being stabbed in the heart? It's enough to drive a woman to apathy. \n\nAnd so it has. It's obvious I have no touch for etiquette despite my heritage, so I won't pretend. I will face the court with something all the rarer- plain faced and indifferent honesty. Call me foolish if you wish, but at least I'm not pretending to be a knight.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24738:        "regency_action": "There's been much focus upon the scramble for Sydney over the past months- it is of course ongoing and will surely result in more death and violence, but I wish to highlight the lighter side to all of you whom have come from across the globe. We, united by our complete foreignness to this place, have a type of freedom never seen- especially here in 2C. It is an opportunity to be celebrated.\n\nThe mortals of Sydney are untouched by fear, innocent and fresh. This, of course, makes feeding easy- but I ask you all to consider that there is other nourishment we can gain from them. Nourishment of ideas, of art and musings. I ask you all to engage with them, and not to smother them out in dominative dismissal- we can use them, after all. Soon, court will be hosted in this wonderful territory of ours- and as the night approaches, I hope to see you all prove that we are growing into something distinct from the rest of the world from which we all came. Paint the alleys! Take the stage! Join a chorus! Fit into the space of untainted mortal expression and feed as you would from their veins!\n\nSoon, more Kine come- and with them, their ignorant and wonderful thoughts. We must take care with them.\n\nThey only live once, after all.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:24785:        "project_4_description": "Whatever Keeper is doing seems big- I know as much from the tremors of the cacophony last month. Given that he has also decided to link himself to me in some manner or another,  that might help in working out his movements and motives- especially if I pump some Auspex into it. \n\nIf I can identify any of- where it is happening, why it is happening, how it is happening, or what the fuck is happening, I'll take it is a win. Especially if it gives me any chance to brace for it.\n\nI have spoken a big game in my letter of reply- that the movement lives in me and thus is unquenchable... but to an extent, I fear- this elder seems something other than Kindred, and he has Charlie at his back. A very dour combination. Perhaps using my understanding of the compulsions of our kind, coupled with my experience of these city streets, I can resist this tyranny of ego and weather what is coming.\n\nI also suspect that Conrad may have received a similar letter- and will be on the lookout for the scrawny bastard. \n\nKeeper has warned me of final death if I'm to interrupt him during the process unannounced... so I won't be going alone. Taking Casmirir along should serve to bolster my chances and keep my beast from doing anything unfortunate if it is so badly effected by whatever Keeper has in store.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:25310:        "personal_story_text": "Carver asks James to take him somewhere that is special to him. Somewhere where James feels is a \"core memeory\".",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:30030:        "project_3_description": "On becoming aware of the existence of an old necropolis Xavier starts the search to find it. He reaches out through his various contacts (foreign and domestic) to look for clues to where it might have been. Searched information on subterranean areas across the history of the city (maps, plans, geological surveys). looking for unusual gaps to information about it being accessed (especially old areas that had been more recently accessed during the time vampires were absent from the city). Looking for folklore about usual events linked to these subterranean sites and immediate surrounds.",
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:31409:          "outcome_summary": "You get wind of a special deceased estate auction of a person who is reputed to be a bon fide soothsayer. You wonder how credible it is, Vaucluse is not known for mystics."
server\scripts\archive\_backups\cycle-id-migration-2026-06-01T05-52-47-723Z.json:32903:              "text": "It's all good in the hood, especially the parties.",
