server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:15:  "clan_goals": "One of the only good things about the Brigadier is that he made her strong and hard to kill- a gangrel. She embraces her heritage but is wary of others, especially elders. This doesn't mean she won't follow them- she's been used to taking orders, it's kept her alive for 25 years. Her main goal is to learn how to shift into animals like her sire.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:154:  "clan_goals": "Conrad is incredibly conservative in his adherence to the Book of Longinus and is incredibly intolerant of those who would stray from its teachings, especially within his own covenant. His goal to maintain ideological purity within his own group and to extinguish any and all blasphemy.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:167:  "indulgences": "Conrad enjoys the theatre, especially musicals, and is able to enjoy them freely as most productions are staged at night.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:255:  "view_traditions": "Brandy sees most traditions and laws as necessary structures, not sacred truths. Having been created as a tool of someone else’s power, she is wary of anything presented as absolute or unquestionable. She respects rules that preserve stability, protect the vulnerable, and prevent senseless cruelty — especially those that keep predators from turning on their own kind without consequence.\n\nHowever, she does not view hierarchy itself as holy. She has seen how propriety and “civilized order” can mask calculated brutality. Laws that exist only to maintain dominance or protect the powerful earn her compliance, but not her reverence.\n\nShe respects the Masquerade and the need for discipline; she fears the unchecked Beast — both her own and others’. What she truly distrusts are systems that demand obedience without meaning. Sacred law, to her, must serve transformation and balance — not vanity or revenge.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:271:  "intolerable": "Brandy does not tolerate cruelty disguised as refinement — calculated harm performed calmly, politely, or for demonstration of power. She has no patience for Kindred who treat suffering as entertainment, status, or proof of superiority.\n\nShe is especially angered by:\n- treating mortals or ghouls as disposable property\n- domination for humiliation rather than necessity\n- feeding used as punishment, spectacle, or control\n- manipulation hidden behind “civilised” manners\n- violation of sacred spaces, rites, or offered trust\n- predation without restraint or responsibility\n\nShe can accept that vampires must hunt. She cannot accept predators who refuse accountability for what they are.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:292:  "view_traditions": "They are useful as long as they can be used to further his motives, especially if he can use information on others breaking them to gain social power over the other.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:337:  "hunting": "Never work with animals or children -- or eat them.  \n\nJack was a heavy user of cocaine back in the day and especially likes to feed off Kine who are high. He will hold and participate in raucous drug-fueled orgies and always offers narcotics to his intended victims.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:343:  "opposed_cov": "The Lance. Jack didn't have much time for priests when he was Kine, he sees no need for them now, especially since he has learned about deeper (Crone) truths that go far beyond the Lance.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:365:  "view_mortals": "They pity ghouls, they logically understand why some kindred may choose to ghoul a mortal but they see it as cheating, the easy way out. Keeping mortals happy, secluded, content and churning along is what Eve has always done best. She sees mortals as having value, especially those within her company. Every single mortal within her company is under her protection, they are the source of her influence, they are her influence and power. Any mortal that would threaten them is seen as lesser and any kindred who would is a threat.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:447:  "intolerable": "Excessive oppression of religious expression, especially towards her own Covenant. People who betray the Crone. Very quick temper over unfounded statements that 'the Crone isn't like that'.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:507:  "indulgences": "As is habitual to the Gorgons, Charles likes working with clay and stone. He participates in artisanal markets which are exclusively at night. Part of his rural estate includes a workshop, kiln and deposits of wild clay. Charles uses these skills and facilities to make ritual items, talismans, artwork for auction, etc. I've reflected this with a Crafts 3 and specialty in sculpting on his character sheet. \n\nHe hates gardening and categorically refuses to cultivate plants. The grounds and grasses of his estate are unkept; full of weeds and wildflowers. \n\nThey are also absolutely infested by snakes.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:565:  "why_covenant": "Ivana didn’t seek it out and wasn’t actively recruited; it just happened. When she rose from being turned, she fled to the sewers that she had been dumped in when she was murdered, and remained hidden there until the denizen's of the Court extracted her and threw her before the Prince and Court. During her time in the sewer, she stayed hidden in the dark, whispering to herself at first, and then to the darkness, begging it for help. Surprisingly, the darkness answered her, and she came to view the darkness as a guardian angel. She displayed an innate affinity for Cruac, and although she didn't pay much attention to it, or grasp the meaning of it all, others noticed - especially Charlie. Aside from her basic education at Court, as part of the bargain struck, when they moved on from Court, Charlie arranged for a contact of his, a Kindred she calls 'Scrambles' or 'Keeper' (Symon), to provide some ongoing support and mentoring. Her arrival in Sydney and attendance at Court would be the first time that she would be in a position to actively engage with her Covenant en masse, and learn more and grow.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:592:  "covenant_factions": "Mac doesn’t perfectly line up with any specific faction, though he’s somewhat similar to the Saboteurs and has weird anti-overlap with the AOA. Where the AOA rejects vampire involvement with mortals, Mac instead sees involvement in mortal affairs as a sort of duty. He doesn’t see vampirism as mystical or special, it’s just another set of talents he should be leveraging for the ideals he believes in.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:602:  "view_traditions": "Mac views the Traditions as practical rules that are generally sensible, but that’s the limit of his respect. He doesn’t care much about laws in general, and he doesn’t see Vampire laws as special.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:618:  "intolerable": "Mac has somewhat idiosyncratic tolerances. He doesn’t like violence targeted at his allies, but he doesn’t really have a principled problem with violence up to and including killing, so long as the target is a combatant of some sort (being a member of a covenant is sufficient to qualify) or otherwise has committed some offence deserving of punishment. He’s especially intolerant of violence towards innocent humans (but again, innocence isn’t all that precise a category). \n\nHe can’t stand slavery or indentured servitude, but doesn’t have qualms about blackmail, intimidation and other hard forms of leverage. \n\nIt’s basically an elaborate version of “All’s fair in love and war”, and it reflects that Mac has a sort of double intensity of the normal ‘frozen in time’ experience most Kindred share: first from his own forced maturity and truncated childhood, then again from his Embrace in the midst of a bitter civil conflict.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:703:  "court_motive": "Kirk’s duties in Sydney are twofold. Firstly, the protection of his Inquisitor, in general. He’s been inseparable from\nConrad for decades, viewing him as his spiritual leader, intellectual superior and benevolent benefactor. Secondly, there is intelligence pointing towards an assassin of the Crones known as the “Grimalkin” that has been dispatched to thwart specifically the heretic hunters of the Sanctified. Kirk’s especially focused on them for the time-being. \n\nIn court, these goals continue, with the added goal of establishing the Lance as a fixture within Sydney.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:704:  "hope_sydney": "Kirk’s duties in Sydney are twofold. Firstly, the protection of his Inquisitor, in general. He’s been inseparable from\nConrad for decades, viewing him as his spiritual leader, intellectual superior and benevolent benefactor. Secondly, there is intelligence pointing towards an assassin of the Crones known as the “Grimalkin” that has been dispatched to thwart specifically the heretic hunters of the Sanctified. Kirk’s especially focused on them for the time-being.",
server\scripts\_ingest-input.json:726:  "intolerable": "Killing someone whose life or unlife has been punctuated by suffering and prejudice  especially without feeding from them or for no good reason.\n\nHe also despises the Crimson Cavalry, and their views, and all who share them.",
